    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Onondaga County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5557A\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the Jamesville-DeWitt central school\ndistrict to discontinue the use of school district-owned parklands and\nto lease such parklands to the town of Onondaga\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nProvides for the establishment of a park district in the town of Ononda-\nga.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 198 of the town law to allow for the estab-\nlishment of a park district in the town of Onondaga.\n\nSection two establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, the Jamesville-Dewitt School District possesses land within\nthe Town of Onondaga that is going unused. In coordination with the Town\nof Onondaga, they wish to be able to lease the land to the town for the\npurpose of constructing a new park. They want to lease as opposed to\nsell to retain the option to utilize the land in the future should\ngrowth of the school district necessitate it. Such an act would require\nthe authorization of the legislature.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
